{
  "meta": {
    "source": "FB Data Download (DYI JSON archive)",
    "chat_name": "Ohana means Family",
    "chat_id": "962639783771350",
    "scraped_at": "2026-05-08",
    "window_start": "2025-11-08",
    "window_end": "2026-05-08",
    "days_covered": 181,
    "total_messages": 1082,
    "total_senders": 6,
    "call_events_filtered": 0,
    "reaction_events_filtered": 0,
    "system_events_filtered": 6,
    "cutoff_reached": true,
    "oldest_msg_seen": "2025-11-08",
    "cutoff_requested": "2025-11-08",
    "archive_file": "facebook-bubakazouba-2026-05-08-otsvpzYw.zip",
    "archive_date_range_in_zip": "2025-05-09 to 2026-05-08",
    "methodology": "Scraped via Messenger CDP (scroll-to-top loop, ~150 passes). EXCLUDED: audio/video call events, group video call tiles, reactions, system messages (join/leave/rename). LINKS detected via: (1) all a[href] in article DOM, (2) regex on full text body, (3) l.messenger.com redirect URLs decoded (u= param). Domain classification via urllib.parse hostname (not substring). Facebook profile mention links excluded.",
    "methodology_v2": "Type classifier v2 applied to raw 635 records. Priority order: gif (forwarded a GIF text) > image (messenger_media anchor OR sent N photos text) > video (facebook.com/share/v/ or share/r/ anchor) > link (any real external URL, profile @mentions excluded) > text (default). Call events excluded upstream. YouTube/IG shares counted as \"link\", not \"video\". Types are mutually exclusive (first match wins).",
    "methodology_v3": "Video classifier v3 (2026-05-05): Split video into subtypes. ZERO direct uploads found -- messenger_media anchors are images only; all prev \"video\" entries were FB link previews, not camera-roll uploads. video_fb = facebook.com/share/v/ (FB native video) OR /share/r/ (FB reel) -- 27 total. video_yt = youtu.be / youtube.com/watch / youtube.com/shorts -- 14 total. video_ig = instagram.com/reel or /p/ -- 2 total. video_uploaded = 0 (none detected; DOM does not expose media type for messenger_media attachments). DOM signatures: FB reel anchor href=facebook.com/share/r/<id>/ with page title as text; YT via l.messenger.com redirect decoded (u= param) to youtu.be/<id>.",
    "methodology_v4": "Re-scrape v4 (2026-05-05): Full history captured via React fiber loadPrevious() loop (CDP). 3359 DOM articles total, 737 window messages (vs 589 prior). @-mention profile URLs (facebook.com/<numeric_id>/) now excluded from FB link counts. video_uploaded=0 confirmed: all messenger_media anchors have imgAlt=\"Open photo\", never \"Open video\". Totals: video_fb=33, video_yt=18, video_ig=2, type_video=53.",
    "methodology_v5": "FB Data Download (DYI) JSON archive -- ground truth, no DOM scraping. Archive: facebook-bubakazouba-2026-05-08-otsvpzYw.zip (1.27 GB, 1 of 1 parts). Thread: ohanameansfamily_962639783771350/message_1.json. 2581 total msgs in archive (2025-05-09 to 2026-05-08), 1082 in 6-month window (excl 6 unsent/deleted). Type classifier: audio > gif > video_uploaded (mp4 direct) > image (photos[]) > share.link domain (video_fb: /reel/ /videos/, video_yt: youtu.be/youtube.com, video_ig: /reel/ /p/) > link_facebook > link_other > text. DOM was blind to: 18 direct video uploads (mp4 camera-roll) which had imgAlt=Open photo in CDP. CDP total 737 vs DYI 1082 = 345 missed messages (47% undercount).",
    "prior_cdp_total": 737,
    "dyi_total": 1082,
    "delta_vs_cdp": 345,
    "methodology_v6": "Reclassification v6 (2026-05-05): Per Sahmoud request, FB reels, FB video shares, YT video links, and IG reel links are now classified as LINK subtypes -- not video. Only m[videos] (real camera-roll MP4 uploads) remain as type=video. New link subtypes: link_fb (old video_fb + old link_facebook = all FB shares), link_yt (old video_yt = YouTube links), link_ig (old video_ig + link_instagram), link_other (old link_other + link_text). link_fb_reel=0 because archive zip was deleted before reel/non-reel split could be applied; all FB shares folded into link_fb. type_totals.link=65 == donut_sum(fb=41+yt=18+ig=0+other=6). Fixes bug: filter Link(18) vs donut Facebook=41 were inconsistent.",
    "methodology_v7": "Topic analysis v7 (2026-05-05): LLM classification (claude-sonnet-4-5) on 326/631 in-window messages with >=3 words of text (remaining 305 are media/reactions/1-2 word). 11 topic labels. Topic initiation: message preceded by >=60min silence = new topic start (205 events from 631 messages). media-share = initiating with image/video/audio (no text extracted). Cosine-similarity rule deferred at this corpus size.",
    "methodology_v8": "Topic analysis v8 (2026-05-09): FB DYI archive re-downloaded (facebook-bubakazouba-2026-05-09-1jOrsfXE.zip, 1.27 GB). 1080 windowed messages (Nov 8, 2025 - May 9, 2026). Filtered to 686 messages with >=3 words text, then excluded 446 FB system messages (joined/started call, sent attachment, reactions etc) leaving 240 real user messages for LLM classification. 11 topic labels: family-coordination, call-coordination, sharing-link, entertainment, religion-islamic, food, health-medical, money-finance, work-school, jokes-memes, other. Topic initiation: >=60min silence = new topic start (243 events). Model: claude-sonnet-4-5, batch size 25.",
    "methodology_v9": "Link subtypes re-classified from FB DYI archive (was deferred in v6 due to deleted zip; now corrected with persistent archive facebook-bubakazouba-2026-05-09-1jOrsfXE.zip). Reel detection: URL path contains /reel/ = fb_reel; all other facebook.com/fb.com = fb. Also corrected: 2 IG links (Aya) previously mislabeled as link_other -- both are instagram.com links (1 via share.link, 1 via content URL regex). link_fb=15, link_fb_reel=26, link_yt=18, link_ig=2, link_other=4. Total link=65 unchanged.",
    "archive_file_v8": "facebook-bubakazouba-2026-05-09-1jOrsfXE.zip",
    "methodology_v10": "Extended analyses v10 (2026-05-05): 8 new sections computed from FB DYI persistent archive. (1) Time-of-day heatmap: 24×7 (hour × day-of-week UTC) per member. (2) Reactions: who gives/receives, emoji preferences, reaction-pair matrix, top-5 viral msgs. (3) Response latency: time-to-first-reply from a different member, avg/median per member (24h cap). (4) Message length: avg/median/p90 word count for text messages; histogram in 5 buckets. (5) Language ratio: per-message heuristic (Arabic U+0600-06FF chars vs Latin alpha); arabic/english/mixed/other. (6) Photo leaderboard: direct uploads (photos[]) per member, album vs single, avg per share. (7) Mention analysis: @Name regex search; FB DYI has no structured mention metadata. (8) Viral messages: top-5 by reaction count.",
    "methodology_v11": "Language detection now distinguishes Franco-Arabic (Arabizi) from English (v11, 2026-05-05). Three buckets: arabic (>50% of letters are Arabic Unicode U+0600-06FF, or >40% in mixed messages), franco_arabic (Latin-dominant but contains Arabizi signals: digit [2,3,5,7,9] sandwiched by letters on both sides, e.g. 5lst/ba2y/ya3ny; OR presence of common Egyptian Arabizi tokens e.g. msh/ana/enta/keda/yalla), english (Latin-dominant, no Arabizi signals). Messages with no letter characters (emoji/punctuation only) are excluded from the percentage denominator. Short ambiguous messages default to english unless Arabizi signals are present."
  },
